@startuml 03-data-model
' SpendSnap — Firestore document model expressed as a class diagram.
' Firestore is schemaless; this is the shape the application consistently writes.

title SpendSnap — Data Model (Firestore document structure)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 6
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  BorderColor #2563EB
  FontColor #0F172A
  AttributeFontColor #334155
}
hide circle

package "users/{userId}" as USERS #F8FAFC {

  class "User (Firebase Auth)" as User {
    +uid : string
    +email : string?  <size:10>(null for guests)</size>
    +isAnonymous : boolean
  }

  class "expenses/{expenseId}" as Expense {
    +amount : number  <size:10>SGD</size>
    +category : "Food"|"Transport"|"Shopping"|"Bills"|"Others"
    +notes : string  <size:10>may be ""</size>
    +date : timestamp  <size:10>serverTimestamp()</size>
    +userId : string  <size:10>== {userId}; used by collection-group reads</size>
    +groupIds : string[]  <size:10>selected groups this expense appears in ([] = personal-only)</size>
  }

  class "settings/monthlyBudget" as Budget {
    +amount : number
    +currency : "SGD"
    +period : "monthly"
    +warningThreshold : number = 0.8
    +exceededThreshold : number = 1
    ..alert de-duplication..
    +alertMonth : string  <size:10>"YYYY-M"</size>
    +alerted80 : boolean
    +alerted100 : boolean
    +updatedAt : timestamp
    +lastCheckedAt : timestamp
  }

  class "settings/groups" as UserGroups {
    +ids : string[]  <size:10>groups the user belongs to</size>
  }
}

package "groups/{groupId}" as GROUPS #FFFBEB {
  class "Group" as Group {
    +name : string  <size:10>owner may rename</size>
    +ownerId : string  <size:10>creator; can rename / archive / delete</size>
    +members : map<uid, true>  <size:10>membership set</size>
    +memberEmails : map<uid, string>  <size:10>denormalised for display</size>
    +createdAt : timestamp
    ..archiving (optional fields)..
    +archived : boolean  <size:10>hidden from active UI for every member</size>
    +archivedAt : timestamp
  }
}

User "1" *-- "0..*" Expense : subcollection\nexpenses/
User "1" *-- "0..1" Budget : subcollection\nsettings/
User "1" *-- "0..1" UserGroups : subcollection\nsettings/

UserGroups "0..*" --> "0..*" Group : ids[] reference\n<size:10>drives callerGroupIds() in rules</size>
Expense "0..*" --> "0..*" Group : groupIds[] tag\n<size:10>array-contains query per group</size>
Group "1" o-- "1..*" User : members map

note bottom of Expense
  **Tagging, not duplication.**
  One document per expense; sharing it with a
  group is a tag in groupIds[]. A group's spend =
  every expense whose groupIds contains its id.

  The author **chooses** the destinations when
  logging (personal-only by default), so a new
  group starts at 0 and past expenses are never
  retroactively re-tagged.
end note

note right of Group
  **Why a map, not an array?**
  members: {uid: true} lets Security Rules test
  `request.auth.uid in resource.data.members`
  and lets a join be a single-key mutation
  that isSelfJoin() can validate.

  memberEmails is denormalised because a client
  cannot resolve another user's email from a uid.

  `archived` is a soft delete: the group and its
  history survive, but it disappears from every
  member's active list and can no longer be joined.
end note

note as IDX #FEF9C3
  **Composite index** (firestore.indexes.json)
  collection group `expenses`
  groupIds ARRAY_CONTAINS + date DESC
end note
IDX .. Expense

@enduml
